  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31404646",
      "title": "How Exactly Does Expo Work?",
      "lectureOrder": 223,
      "videoOrder": 217,
      "sourceHash": "9895a6a95eb2fab87919fe79f089dc8cebc69ce5ef0741c19d7b3a2f8a740d0f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.43,
          "end": 4.98,
          "en": "So, before we dive into any demos,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.98,
          "end": 9.05,
          "en": "and we dive into different apps built in different ways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.05,
          "end": 13.78,
          "en": "let's understand how Expo actually worked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.78,
          "end": 18.07,
          "en": "Now, of course, we used Expo init to create expo projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 18.07,
          "end": 20.76,
          "en": "We did that in the first course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.76,
          "end": 24.37,
          "en": "And then we used this Expo Go app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.37,
          "end": 26.77,
          "en": "which we could install on a real device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.77,
          "end": 30.9,
          "en": "or which was installed for us on the emulators as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.9,
          "end": 33.8,
          "en": "to preview our app during development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.8,
          "end": 38.76,
          "en": "And this indeed is a crucial aspect of using Expo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.76,
          "end": 41.23,
          "en": "It makes development that easy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.23,
          "end": 44.66,
          "en": "because Expo installs this extra app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.66,
          "end": 47.94,
          "en": "this extra runtime on a device,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.94,
          "end": 50.83,
          "en": "on an emulator or a real device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.83,
          "end": 53.99,
          "en": "And during development, when you write your code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.99,
          "end": 57.4,
          "en": "that code is loaded by Expo into that app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.4,
          "end": 60.15,
          "en": "and executed there, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.15,
          "end": 63.61,
          "en": "which means that you can instantly preview your code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.61,
          "end": 65.63,
          "en": "you don't have to install your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.63,
          "end": 69.41,
          "en": "or build your code as an app, and then install that app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.41,
          "end": 71.89,
          "en": "Instead you have the Expo Go app installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.89,
          "end": 75.32,
          "en": "and you can preview your code just like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.32,
          "end": 77.44200000000001,
          "en": "This gives us all the advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.44200000000001,
          "end": 80.23,
          "en": "that we can just install this Expo Go app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.23,
          "end": 83.35,
          "en": "from the Google Play Store or the Apple App Store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.35,
          "end": 87.78,
          "en": "onto any device of our choice, onto our iPhone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.78,
          "end": 92.3,
          "en": "onto any Android device, on a phone of one of our friends.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.3,
          "end": 96.38,
          "en": "And we can then preview the app there during development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.38,
          "end": 99.52000000000001,
          "en": "without building it, publishing it, or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.52000000000001,
          "end": 102.363,
          "en": "And that makes development super easy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.36,
          "end": 106.08,
          "en": "Now, what is worth noting, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.08,
          "end": 110.42,
          "en": "is that during development when using this Expo approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.42,
          "end": 112.52000000000001,
          "en": "as we used it in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.52000000000001,
          "end": 116.19,
          "en": "you don't build real app executables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.19,
          "end": 120.07,
          "en": "You don't build standalone apps that would be installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.07,
          "end": 124.52,
          "en": "on the emulators or on any phones or devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.52,
          "end": 127.01,
          "en": "Instead, it's really just that source code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.01,
          "end": 131.63,
          "en": "that is loaded or injected into that Expo Go client app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.63,
          "end": 133.72,
          "en": "and then executed there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.72,
          "end": 138.72,
          "en": "But you can still build and publish standalone apps, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 139.1,
          "end": 141.66,
          "en": "This does not mean that when you build an app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.66,
          "end": 143.92000000000002,
          "en": "it only runs in the Expo Go app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.92000000000002,
          "end": 146.88,
          "en": "This is a helper during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.88,
          "end": 149.87,
          "en": "but of course, once you're done building your app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.87,
          "end": 152.75,
          "en": "when using the approach we used in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.75,
          "end": 155.77,
          "en": "you will still be able to build your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.77,
          "end": 158.99,
          "en": "and publish your app as a standalone app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.99,
          "end": 163.45,
          "en": "so that users of your app won't need the Expo Go app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.45,
          "end": 166.67000000000002,
          "en": "It's really just a helper during development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.67000000000002,
          "end": 169.07999999999998,
          "en": "And in the next course section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.07999999999998,
          "end": 171.62,
          "en": "when we dive into publishing apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.62,
          "end": 174.49,
          "en": "you will learn how you can publish apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.49,
          "end": 176.57999999999998,
          "en": "as we build them in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.57999999999998,
          "end": 179.67000000000002,
          "en": "as standalone iOS or Android apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 179.67000000000002,
          "end": 183.55,
          "en": "that do not depend on the Expo Go app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.55,
          "end": 185.57,
          "en": "So Expo gives us this helper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.57,
          "end": 188.76,
          "en": "but still allows us to publish standalone apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.76,
          "end": 190.56,
          "en": "and this is really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.56,
          "end": 193.72,
          "en": "You can still build and publish standalone apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.72,
          "end": 195.66,
          "en": "which are independent of Expo Go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.66,
          "end": 200.64,
          "en": "And this will be done with help of a service, EAS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.64,
          "end": 203.96,
          "en": "at which we'll take a closer look in the next course section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.96,
          "end": 207.31,
          "en": "which helps us build those standalone apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.31,
          "end": 209.5,
          "en": "Therefore, we really have to differentiate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.5,
          "end": 212.97,
          "en": "between the environment we have during development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.97,
          "end": 215.19,
          "en": "and the app we get for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.19,
          "end": 217.87,
          "en": "So when we're finished and during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.87,
          "end": 222.02,
          "en": "we can move fast and get instant previews on any device,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.02,
          "end": 224.21,
          "en": "thanks to this Expo Go app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 224.21,
          "end": 227.77,
          "en": "And we simply use this shared runtime, this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 227.77,
          "end": 231.32,
          "en": "to load our code and reflect changes whenever we make them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231.32,
          "end": 232.62,
          "en": "And for production,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.62,
          "end": 236.32,
          "en": "we can still build lean, independent, standalone apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.32,
          "end": 238.85,
          "en": "that don't need this Expo Go app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.85,
          "end": 241.29,
          "en": "And with help of this build service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 241.29,
          "end": 244.4,
          "en": "which we're going to learn about in the next course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.4,
          "end": 247.7,
          "en": "we can even build those apps for any platform.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 247.7,
          "end": 251.34,
          "en": "So we can even build iOS apps if we're on a windows machine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.34,
          "end": 255.19,
          "en": "which would not be possible if we had to build them locally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 255.19,
          "end": 257.32,
          "en": "But again, that is something we will explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.32,
          "end": 258.83299999999997,
          "en": "in the next course section.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
